:: WalkingTrail [nobr]
<<HUD>>
<<set $trailVisits += 1>>

<<if $trailVisits is 1>>
<div class="prose-block">
<p>A tree-lined path winding between mature oaks, a small pond off to one side, benches spaced out along the loop. Joggers and dog walkers in the distance. The kind of ordinary, well-worn beauty you stop noticing after the third time you almost got evicted.</p>
</div>
<<else>>
<div class="prose-block">
<p>Same loop, same trees, same pond throwing back whatever light the sky&apos;s handing out today.</p>
</div>
<</if>>

<<if $trailVisits is 3>>

<<SceneDivider "The Old Man on the Bench">>

<div class="prose-block">
<p>There&apos;s an old man on the bench by the pond. He&apos;s here every time you come. Different book each time. He&apos;s never acknowledged you directly, but this time, without looking up:</p>
</div>

<<Dialogue "Old Man" "📖" "You walk like someone learning to live in a new country." "">>
<<Dialogue "You" "😳" "...What?" "you">>
<<Dialogue "Old Man" "📖" "I lived in four countries before I was thirty. Every time, the first thing you learn is how to walk. Where to put your feet. How to hold your shoulders. You're learning. I can tell." "">>
<<Dialogue "You" "🙂" "What book are you reading?" "you">>
<<Dialogue "Old Man" "📖" "Ovid. Metamorphoses. Stories about people who transform into something new." "">>

<div class="prose-block">
<p>He glances at you over his reading glasses. The faintest smile.</p>
</div>

<<Dialogue "Old Man" "📖" "You might like it." "">>

<div class="prose-block">
<p>He never gives his name. You never tell him yours, or your story. He never asks. But every time you pass now, he nods, and that nod means: <em>I see you. You&apos;re doing fine.</em></p>
</div>

<<set $metOldMan to true>>
<<run window.rbAddMilestone("The Old Man on the Bench noticed you.")>>

<<elseif $metOldMan>>

<div class="prose-block">
<p>The old man is on his bench, a different book today. He glances up as you pass. Nods. Goes back to reading.</p>
</div>

<</if>>

<<if $day gte 3 and not $seenParkNeedAir>>

<<ImagePlaceholder "An empty bench beside the pond, afternoon light" "banner" "assets/locations/park/bench.png">>

<div class="prose-block">
<p>I needed air. The apartment walls were closing in, shrinking by the hour, the ceiling stain getting bigger as the rooms got smaller. Two days inside and my skin felt like it had been wrapped in cling film.</p>
<p>A woman jogs past, ponytail swinging, wireless earbuds, tank top over a sports bra, leggings that cost more than my rent. She looks effortless, like she's been running in this body her whole life, like her legs have always been that shape and her breasts have always been contained in that particular sports bra that fits perfectly because she was fitted at a store by someone who taught her the lean-and-scoop technique when she was fourteen.</p>
<p>I watch her disappear around the curve of the path and feel something that isn&apos;t envy exactly. Closer to yearning. She knows how to be a woman the way Marcus knew how to be a man, instinctively, unconsciously, without thinking about every gesture and every article of clothing.</p>
<p>I&apos;ll get there. Maybe. Someday. Right now I&apos;m a woman the way someone who just got their driver&apos;s license is a driver. Technically qualified. Functionally terrified.</p>
<p>A squirrel runs across the path in front of me and stops to stare, head tilted, like I&apos;m the strangest thing it&apos;s seen all day.</p>
<p>&quot;Same, buddy,&quot; I tell it. &quot;Same.&quot;</p>
</div>

<<set $seenParkNeedAir to true>>

<</if>>

<<if $day gte 3 and not $metDuckLady and window.rbRandom(1, 10) lte 4>>

<<SceneDivider "The Duck Lady">>

<<ImagePlaceholder "An elderly woman on a park bench feeding bread crusts to ducks" "float" "assets/characters/supporting/duck-lady.png">>

<div class="prose-block">
<p>An older woman sits down on the other end of my bench with a paper bag of bread crusts, tearing them into pieces and throwing them to the ducks in the pond.</p>
<p>She glances at me. &quot;You look like you&apos;re carrying the weight of the world, sweetheart.&quot;</p>
<p>I almost laugh. If she only knew.</p>
<p>&quot;Just thinking.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;Well, don&apos;t do too much of that. It&apos;s bad for you.&quot; She tosses a crust. A duck waddles over and grabs it before a pigeon can. &quot;My husband used to say thinking is just worrying with a college degree.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;Smart man.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;Dead man,&quot; she says cheerfully, the way people say it when the grief has aged into something softer, rounded at the edges. &quot;But he was right about most things. You eat lunch today?&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;Yeah.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;Good. Girls your age forget to eat. My granddaughter, she lives on coffee and anxiety. I tell her, &apos;Marina, your body is not a suggestion.&apos; She doesn&apos;t listen.&quot; She throws another crust. &quot;Nobody listens.&quot;</p>
<p>A duck quacks. The old woman smiles at it with genuine affection.</p>
<p>&quot;You have a good day, sweetheart. Whatever you&apos;re carrying, put it down for five minutes and watch the ducks. They don&apos;t care about your problems, and that&apos;s the most relaxing thing in the world.&quot;</p>
<p>She gets up, folds the empty bread bag neatly, and walks away.</p>
<p>I watch the ducks for five minutes. She was right. They don&apos;t care about my problems. They&apos;re concerned exclusively with bread crusts, pond algae, and the complex social dynamics of duck life.</p>
<p>I feel slightly better. Not fixed. But better.</p>
</div>

<<set $metDuckLady to true>>
<<run window.statChange("stress", -5)>>

<</if>>

<<if $day is 2 and window.rbRandom(1, 10) lte 3>>

<div class="prose-block">
<p>A woman pushing a stroller passes me on the path. The baby inside is asleep, mouth open, fists clenched, wearing a onesie with a dinosaur on it. The woman looks exhausted in the specific way new parents look exhausted, beyond tired into some new dimension of consciousness that runs entirely on caffeine and love.</p>
<p>She sees me looking at the baby and smiles. &quot;Eight weeks. I haven&apos;t slept since March.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;She&apos;s beautiful.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;He, actually. The dinosaur is misleading.&quot; She laughs. &quot;I&apos;m running out of clean onesies. Everything is a crisis at this point.&quot;</p>
<p>She walks on and the baby doesn&apos;t stir at all.</p>
<p>I stand on the path and put my hand on my lower belly. Not for any specific reason, not because I&apos;m pregnant or even thinking about pregnancy. Just because my body has a uterus now, ovaries, fallopian tubes, the theoretical capacity to grow a person inside it, and that fact hits me at random moments like this, watching a stranger push a stroller down a path I&apos;ve walked a hundred times as a man who never once thought about wombs.</p>
<p>I take my hand away and keep walking. But the feeling stays, the awareness of possibility, of a body that can do things I never once imagined it doing.</p>
</div>

<<set $player.fem to Math.clamp($player.fem + 1, 0, 100)>>

<</if>>

<div class="action-list">

<<link '<span class="action-icon">🏃</span><span class="action-text">Jog the loop<span class="action-sub">Lungs burning, legs unfamiliar, keep going</span></span>' "WalkingTrail">>
	<<set $player.fit to Math.clamp($player.fit + 2, 0, 100)>>
	<<set $player.stress to Math.clamp($player.stress - 3, 0, 100)>>
	<<set $player.energy to Math.clamp($player.energy - 10, 0, 100)>>
<</link>>

<<link '<span class="action-icon">🚶</span><span class="action-text">Walk the loop<span class="action-sub">No agenda, just moving</span></span>' "WalkingTrail">>
	<<set $player.stress to Math.clamp($player.stress - 3, 0, 100)>>
	<<set $player.energy to Math.clamp($player.energy - 4, 0, 100)>>
<</link>>

<<link '<span class="action-icon">🪑</span><span class="action-text">Sit on a bench and think<span class="action-sub">Watch the pond do nothing in particular</span></span>' "WalkingTrail">>
	<<set $player.stress to Math.clamp($player.stress - 5, 0, 100)>>
<</link>>

<<link '<span class="action-icon">🤸</span><span class="action-text">Stretch<span class="action-sub">Everything about this body moves differently now</span></span>' "WalkingTrail">>
	<<set $player.fit to Math.clamp($player.fit + 1, 0, 100)>>
<</link>>

</div>

<div class="choice-block" style="margin-top:2rem;">
	<<link '<span>← Back outside</span>' "Outside">><</link>>
</div>
